Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, kio
Recommends: imagemagick, ffmpeg, poppler-utils, python3-gi
Description: fork of Dolphin that rethinks how you work with your files
 Dolphin NG is a fork of KDE's Dolphin: cards and drawn rows that tell what a
 file is at a glance, quick filters by kind of file, groups that follow the
 sorting, quick actions one click away, and work in progress shown on the files
 themselves.
 .
 It installs under /opt/ng/dolphin-ng, next to Ubuntu's Dolphin, which stays the
 default file manager: start it as "Dolphin NG" from the menu, or with the
 dolphin-ng command.
